1
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:07,412
I want Mariko to smile.

2
00:00:09,013 --> 00:00:10,115
That's all.

3
00:00:10,815 --> 00:00:12,450
She's in the way.

4
00:00:12,517 --> 00:00:14,152
She's just like her mother.

5
00:00:14,219 --> 00:00:14,886
NOZAWA CONSTRUCTION

6
00:00:14,953 --> 00:00:15,987
It was you, wasn't it?

7
00:00:16,921 --> 00:00:18,189
You're the one who killed Tateiwa.

8
00:00:18,256 --> 00:00:21,826
I wonder how everyone would feel
if they found out who you really are.

9
00:00:21,893 --> 00:00:23,595
I wonder what Mariko would think too.

10
00:01:04,302 --> 00:01:08,940
‎TAISUKE SAKURA

11
00:01:41,606 --> 00:01:42,674
Is this you?

12
00:01:47,111 --> 00:01:49,314
You've been following
my social media for years,

13
00:01:50,114 --> 00:01:52,550
before we even met?

14
00:01:55,019 --> 00:01:57,655
What? What does this mean?

15
00:02:01,826 --> 00:02:02,660
Well…

16
00:02:11,803 --> 00:02:12,837
Up until now…

17
00:02:15,206 --> 00:02:17,942
I just thought you were someone
who happened to share my interests.

18
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:21,412
Visiting cafes is one of my hobbies.

19
00:02:21,913 --> 00:02:24,148
I'm a huge Marvel fan.

20
00:02:24,215 --> 00:02:25,683
You somehow

21
00:02:27,085 --> 00:02:29,420
always appear when I want you to.

22
00:02:31,689 --> 00:02:34,492
You say things like
you've known me forever.

23
00:02:35,493 --> 00:02:37,295
I always thought
you were a strange person.

24
00:02:38,463 --> 00:02:39,297
But…

25
00:02:40,598 --> 00:02:44,636
So none of that was a coincidence?

26
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:47,605
You were looking into me ahead of time?

27
00:02:53,811 --> 00:02:56,214
Hey, say something!

28
00:02:58,850 --> 00:02:59,684
I'm sorry.

29
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:03,955
You're sorry…

30
00:03:11,496 --> 00:03:13,197
Mariko, please wait.

31
00:03:14,766 --> 00:03:15,767
Mariko.

32
00:03:26,344 --> 00:03:27,211
I'm sorry.

33
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:19,630
Yukimura.

34
00:04:26,971 --> 00:04:28,773
An incident has occurred,

35
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:32,276
and someone who looked like you
was caught on the dashcam

36
00:04:33,077 --> 00:04:35,012
of a car parked near the scene.

37
00:04:36,881 --> 00:04:38,616
We would like to ask you some questions.

38
00:04:38,683 --> 00:04:40,685
Could you please
accompany us to the station?

39
00:04:43,121 --> 00:04:44,222
What kind of incident?

40
00:04:52,196 --> 00:04:53,064
Step over here.

41
00:05:03,775 --> 00:05:05,510
Sayuri Nose…

42
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:10,348
has been found dead.

43
00:05:18,923 --> 00:05:21,259
FATHER

44
00:05:47,151 --> 00:05:48,352
This

45
00:05:49,487 --> 00:05:52,857
shows you and Sayuri Nose
entering the alley.

46
00:05:54,192 --> 00:05:55,226
And this one

47
00:05:55,993 --> 00:06:00,097
shows the person who first discovered
the scene entering the alley.

48
00:06:01,466 --> 00:06:04,235
During this gap, Sayuri Nose was murdered.

49
00:06:07,505 --> 00:06:09,740
The circumstantial evidence is complete.

50
00:06:09,807 --> 00:06:11,209
-Why…
-Hm?

51
00:06:13,444 --> 00:06:15,746
No, I mean,
why does it line up so perfectly?

52
00:06:16,881 --> 00:06:18,950
You were present at the scene

53
00:06:19,884 --> 00:06:23,488
of two murders,
Tateiwa's and Sayuri Nose's.

54
00:06:23,554 --> 00:06:28,159
I don't believe those can be seen
as mere coincidences.

55
00:06:33,731 --> 00:06:34,932
Is the world…

56
00:06:36,868 --> 00:06:39,871
really so full of coincidences?

57
00:06:41,272 --> 00:06:44,575
Much like your relationship
with Mariko Nose.

58
00:06:47,378 --> 00:06:48,312
What are you talking about?

59
00:06:48,846 --> 00:06:50,414
You and Mariko

60
00:06:51,315 --> 00:06:52,917
went to the same middle school,

61
00:06:53,618 --> 00:06:54,452
high school,

62
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,522
university,

63
00:06:58,689 --> 00:07:00,958
and now are working at the same company.

64
00:07:02,927 --> 00:07:03,794
Yes.

65
00:07:04,395 --> 00:07:07,131
You say this is all a coincidence?

66
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,936
Does this have anything to do
with Sayuri being murdered?

67
00:07:13,571 --> 00:07:16,807
It is an important piece
in proving your motive.

68
00:07:27,818 --> 00:07:32,590
To answer your previous question,
I don't think so.

69
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:39,363
Coincidences don't just happen
that easily.

70
00:07:41,132 --> 00:07:44,802
Everything that seems like a coincidence
usually has some intent behind it.

71
00:07:46,437 --> 00:07:48,973
Sometimes, people wish
it was a coincidence,

72
00:07:50,374 --> 00:07:52,343
or people fail to see the hidden reason

73
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:54,445
and assume something happened
just because.

74
00:07:58,683 --> 00:08:01,252
The fact that I was present
at two murder scenes…

75
00:08:02,186 --> 00:08:03,354
I think it was also due

76
00:08:04,889 --> 00:08:07,992
to someone's intention,

77
00:08:09,327 --> 00:08:12,229
someone pulling the strings.

78
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:17,768
Really?

79
00:08:20,438 --> 00:08:21,372
Who could it be?

80
00:08:24,275 --> 00:08:25,876
I'd like to know that myself.

81
00:08:39,156 --> 00:08:40,758
Um, uh,

82
00:08:40,825 --> 00:08:45,963
so in other words, you did
what you did to protect Mariko,

83
00:08:46,030 --> 00:08:49,533
-Tateiwa, and Sayuri, right?
-Yes.

84
00:08:50,167 --> 00:08:52,937
You dug up dirt on those two
and threatened them.

85
00:08:53,504 --> 00:08:56,040
Yes. I swear to God, that's all I did.

86
00:08:56,607 --> 00:08:58,709
Man, that's already problematic enough.

87
00:08:59,644 --> 00:09:02,146
-I'm sorry.
-Why are you apologizing to me?

88
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:04,015
Sorry…

89
00:09:08,486 --> 00:09:10,321
There's too much stuff to think about.

90
00:09:10,955 --> 00:09:12,456
First off,

91
00:09:12,523 --> 00:09:14,859
Mariko found out
about your account, right?

92
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:17,328
I guess it freaked her out?

93
00:09:21,966 --> 00:09:24,201
Hm, probably…

94
00:09:25,136 --> 00:09:26,637
And during that,

95
00:09:26,704 --> 00:09:29,440
the police took you in for questioning,
right in front of her.

96
00:09:32,977 --> 00:09:35,246
No, no, it's fine!

97
00:09:35,312 --> 00:09:37,248
If you explain it, she'll understand.

98
00:09:37,314 --> 00:09:39,216
It's impossible. I can't explain it.

99
00:09:39,283 --> 00:09:40,685
But you have to.

100
00:09:41,485 --> 00:09:44,955
You don't want to lose
your 25-year love, do you?

101
00:09:46,857 --> 00:09:50,528
But it's impossible.

102
00:09:55,866 --> 00:09:57,168
Why were you following her?

103
00:10:00,071 --> 00:10:00,905
What?

104
00:10:01,806 --> 00:10:04,208
You could have used a different account
or just lurked without following.

105
00:10:04,842 --> 00:10:07,678
You didn't have to go,
"Oh, a new post! Like!"

106
00:10:09,914 --> 00:10:13,451
I knew about Mariko's social media account
right when she created it.

107
00:10:14,018 --> 00:10:17,521
But I thought it'd be bad to follow her
right away, so I waited for a few months.

108
00:10:18,989 --> 00:10:22,493
At first, I was afraid
that if a stranger followed her,

109
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,028
she'd be creeped out.

110
00:10:25,129 --> 00:10:27,198
But getting to hear
Mariko's inner thoughts,

111
00:10:27,264 --> 00:10:30,301
which I never could have known before,
expressed directly by her,

112
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:31,736
it was an unbelievable experience.

113
00:10:32,303 --> 00:10:34,772
And being able to reply with a "like"…

114
00:10:36,741 --> 00:10:38,676
Mariko seeing my "like"…

115
00:10:40,077 --> 00:10:42,580
It was just incredible.

116
00:10:44,749 --> 00:10:49,353
And before I knew it, I was liking

117
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,422
every single post she made…

118
00:10:53,758 --> 00:10:54,625
I'm sorry.

119
00:10:54,692 --> 00:10:56,393
I told you, don't apologize to me.

120
00:10:58,863 --> 00:10:59,730
Well, whatever.

121
00:11:00,698 --> 00:11:01,766
More importantly, the issue now is--

122
00:11:01,832 --> 00:11:03,567
Is Mariko okay?

123
00:11:03,634 --> 00:11:06,237
Huh? Even at a time like this,
that's what you're worried about?

124
00:11:07,037 --> 00:11:11,108
Those two were clearly
showing hostility toward her.

125
00:11:12,443 --> 00:11:14,445
What was the reason they were killed?

126
00:11:16,013 --> 00:11:17,782
What if the killer's target is Mariko?

127
00:11:37,835 --> 00:11:44,742
LEARN MORE ABOUT SLEEP

128
00:11:44,809 --> 00:11:46,010
-Oh…
-Here.

129
00:11:46,076 --> 00:11:47,011
Thank you.

130
00:11:55,886 --> 00:11:56,887
Keito.

131
00:12:11,368 --> 00:12:12,303
Father.

132
00:12:28,052 --> 00:12:30,387
Earlier today around six a.m.,

133
00:12:30,454 --> 00:12:34,225
a woman was reported lying prone
on the riverbank

134
00:12:34,825 --> 00:12:38,229
under an elevated structure
in Setagaya Ward.

135
00:12:38,963 --> 00:12:41,899
The deceased has been identified
as Sayuri Nose,

136
00:12:41,966 --> 00:12:45,202
wife of Ginjiro Nose,
president of major cosmetics firm

137
00:12:45,269 --> 00:12:46,503
Nose Cosmetics.

138
00:12:47,371 --> 00:12:50,507
Marks suggesting strangulation
were found on Sayuri's neck,

139
00:12:50,574 --> 00:12:54,111
and police are investigating
the case as a homicide.

140
00:12:54,612 --> 00:12:57,514
Regarding Nose Cosmetics, one month ago…

141
00:12:58,849 --> 00:13:03,587
So that's why Mariko was absent yesterday.

142
00:13:04,722 --> 00:13:07,391
Isn't this insane? Like, seriously scary.

143
00:13:09,693 --> 00:13:12,596
-Good morning.
-Mariko…

144
00:13:21,772 --> 00:13:25,676
I'm sorry for causing
everyone such concern.

145
00:13:27,111 --> 00:13:29,446
And for taking a sudden day off yesterday.

146
00:13:29,513 --> 00:13:31,982
-Mariko, you don't need to apologize.
-I mean,

147
00:13:32,049 --> 00:13:33,784
-what's the situation actually like?
-Stop.

148
00:13:34,518 --> 00:13:35,653
Ah, it's fine.

149
00:13:36,353 --> 00:13:39,456
But honestly, we haven't been told
much more than what's on the news either.

150
00:13:40,124 --> 00:13:43,127
Mariko, you can take today off too.

151
00:13:43,861 --> 00:13:44,995
I can't do that.

152
00:13:45,729 --> 00:13:49,133
Besides, the internal company presentation
is soon. We need to hurry and prepare.

153
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,001
-Yes.
-Yes.

154
00:13:51,669 --> 00:13:53,203
Thank you all.

155
00:13:54,805 --> 00:13:55,839
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

156
00:13:57,574 --> 00:14:00,978
Hashimoto, for the 3 p.m.
promotional strategy meeting…

157
00:14:01,045 --> 00:14:04,415
Eleven through three are promising,

158
00:14:05,716 --> 00:14:08,886
-but with 11…
-Uh, regarding number six…

159
00:14:08,953 --> 00:14:10,321
There could be 1.58 million…

160
00:14:10,888 --> 00:14:13,424
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

161
00:14:25,169 --> 00:14:26,070
Mariko.

162
00:14:27,504 --> 00:14:31,642
Um, about what happened
the day before yesterday…

163
00:14:31,709 --> 00:14:33,043
Sorry, but…

164
00:14:34,311 --> 00:14:35,713
too much has been happening.

165
00:14:35,779 --> 00:14:37,181
My mind is a mess right now.

166
00:14:38,048 --> 00:14:39,483
I don't want to think about anything.

167
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:44,154
I'm sorry.

168
00:15:06,677 --> 00:15:08,379
My 32 years of life

169
00:15:09,046 --> 00:15:11,548
were short, but fulfilling.

170
00:15:12,483 --> 00:15:13,417
Mariko.

171
00:15:14,218 --> 00:15:15,252
Please stay well.

172
00:15:15,919 --> 00:15:19,156
Walk over my fallen body
and find happiness.

173
00:15:23,127 --> 00:15:25,195
The higher-ups said it was suicide.

174
00:15:25,262 --> 00:15:27,965
We can't do anything after that.

175
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:33,637
No, I can't die yet.

176
00:15:39,043 --> 00:15:40,677
Even if I am to die,

177
00:15:41,245 --> 00:15:43,781
it'll be after I've ensured
Mariko's safety and happiness.

178
00:15:56,493 --> 00:15:58,028
Um, excuse me.

179
00:15:59,797 --> 00:16:02,299
Why did you put those flowers there?

180
00:16:03,901 --> 00:16:09,506
A long time ago, a regular customer
of my shop had an accident here.

181
00:16:10,074 --> 00:16:11,241
Your shop…

182
00:16:12,109 --> 00:16:14,711
I run a flower shop nearby.

183
00:16:17,314 --> 00:16:19,817
It's a white flower about this big!

184
00:16:19,883 --> 00:16:20,884
Is it this one?

185
00:16:20,951 --> 00:16:23,520
No, not that. A white one, about this big…

186
00:16:32,362 --> 00:16:34,698
FUSAIDO FLOWER SHOP

187
00:16:34,765 --> 00:16:36,100
You know who the culprit might be?

188
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:37,734
Yes.

189
00:16:38,802 --> 00:16:40,204
My daughter Mariko was the victim

190
00:16:40,270 --> 00:16:42,739
of an attempted kidnapping
when she was little.

191
00:16:45,476 --> 00:16:47,311
The Satoru Hatano case, right?

192
00:16:48,245 --> 00:16:52,616
I was still a university student
back then, but I remember the case well.

193
00:16:53,317 --> 00:16:56,620
I suspect that both Tateiwa and my wife

194
00:16:57,488 --> 00:17:00,457
were killed by this man, Hatano.

195
00:17:01,225 --> 00:17:05,896
Actually, I haven't been able to contact
my secretary, Asai, for a while.

196
00:17:07,231 --> 00:17:09,199
I've been receiving emails
from him, though.

197
00:17:10,667 --> 00:17:14,605
His mother back home is doing fine.

198
00:17:14,671 --> 00:17:16,640
Asai hasn't returned there.

199
00:17:18,575 --> 00:17:21,111
Also, this was left on his desk.

200
00:17:22,846 --> 00:17:26,083
It seems to belong
to the editor of this article.

201
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:30,354
Hatano must be involved
in Asai's disappearance.

202
00:17:32,356 --> 00:17:33,991
I understand the situation.

203
00:17:35,092 --> 00:17:36,693
I will take action on my end.

204
00:17:37,427 --> 00:17:38,562
Thank you very much.

205
00:17:40,764 --> 00:17:42,099
Please stop.

206
00:17:42,166 --> 00:17:44,201
SETAGAYA CASE

207
00:17:44,268 --> 00:17:46,937
You must also be worried
about Mariko's safety.

208
00:17:53,043 --> 00:17:54,845
Leave it to me.

209
00:18:01,785 --> 00:18:06,857
I don't know anything about that.

210
00:18:09,593 --> 00:18:12,262
You've been a secretary
at that company for 25 years.

211
00:18:12,329 --> 00:18:13,864
There's no way you don't know.

212
00:18:13,931 --> 00:18:16,166
No, I really don't.

213
00:18:17,267 --> 00:18:18,936
Useless.

214
00:18:19,002 --> 00:18:21,238
No point in keeping you alive then.

215
00:18:21,305 --> 00:18:24,074
What are you planning to do?

216
00:18:26,543 --> 00:18:30,414
Well, you see, I want to meet him.

217
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:34,952
You can't just alter someone's life
and never meet them face to face, right?

218
00:18:36,019 --> 00:18:37,688
If it wasn't for that kid,

219
00:18:38,222 --> 00:18:40,290
I wouldn't have been caught.

220
00:18:41,158 --> 00:18:44,161
I need to give a proper
token of appreciation

221
00:18:45,028 --> 00:18:49,566
to that brave young boy
who saved the little princess.

222
00:18:58,775 --> 00:19:02,546
Hello? Yes, that's right.

223
00:19:02,613 --> 00:19:04,381
I'll pay the money.

224
00:19:04,448 --> 00:19:06,950
Yukimura, I need to talk to you.

225
00:19:07,451 --> 00:19:08,352
Yes?

226
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,855
Yukimura, you are

227
00:19:12,422 --> 00:19:14,258
that boy who saved Mariko
back then, right?

228
00:19:14,992 --> 00:19:16,960
Years ago, on behalf of the president,

229
00:19:17,027 --> 00:19:19,162
I visited your parents
to express our gratitude.

230
00:19:20,931 --> 00:19:22,432
Could you keep this a secret?

231
00:19:23,467 --> 00:19:25,602
I don't want Mariko to find out.

232
00:19:25,669 --> 00:19:26,637
Please.

233
00:19:38,315 --> 00:19:40,784
SETAGAYA KIDNAPPING CASE DETAILS

234
00:19:46,256 --> 00:19:47,891
MARIKO NOSE - ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STUDENT

235
00:19:47,958 --> 00:19:50,594
ALMOST TAKEN AWAY BY A STRANGER

236
00:19:50,661 --> 00:19:51,728
SHE SCREAMED FOR SOMEONE TO HELP

237
00:19:54,698 --> 00:19:57,167
COLOR OF THE VEHICLE WAS BLACK

238
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:03,173
SOTA YUKIMURA - ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STUDENT

239
00:20:30,701 --> 00:20:33,570
Excuse me. Here's this month's sales data.

240
00:20:33,637 --> 00:20:35,505
-Please check it.
-Okay.

241
00:21:01,164 --> 00:21:02,065
-Sorry.
-I'm sorry.

242
00:21:03,033 --> 00:21:05,302
Please check this.

243
00:21:05,869 --> 00:21:06,737
Okay.

244
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:15,779
Which type of plastic
would be best for this?

245
00:21:20,050 --> 00:21:23,620
For that, recycled PET would be best.

246
00:21:25,422 --> 00:21:27,224
Recycled PET?

247
00:21:28,725 --> 00:21:31,495
Well, biomass plastic
is also an attractive choice,

248
00:21:31,561 --> 00:21:33,897
but it might be more difficult to manage.

249
00:21:34,564 --> 00:21:37,401
I think recycled PET, which has
a proven record, would be best,

250
00:21:37,467 --> 00:21:38,769
considering our schedule.

251
00:21:39,336 --> 00:21:40,303
I see.

252
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:42,773
Well, it looks good for sustainability.

253
00:21:42,839 --> 00:21:44,474
It doesn't really give off a luxury feel.

254
00:21:44,541 --> 00:21:47,778
Okay then, for example,
instead of 100% recycled PET,

255
00:21:47,844 --> 00:21:51,581
-we could use 30%.
-Yeah, I see.

256
00:22:13,570 --> 00:22:14,604
Mariko.

257
00:22:15,972 --> 00:22:19,643
I want to talk about
what happened the other day.

258
00:22:21,878 --> 00:22:24,748
Do you have time after this?

259
00:22:45,035 --> 00:22:47,170
What are you doing here? What happened?

260
00:22:47,237 --> 00:22:48,505
Are you finished with work?

261
00:22:49,673 --> 00:22:50,607
Yes.

262
00:22:50,674 --> 00:22:51,675
I'll give you a ride.

263
00:22:52,242 --> 00:22:53,109
‎What?

264
00:22:53,176 --> 00:22:56,079
I'll explain the details later. Come on.

265
00:23:18,368 --> 00:23:19,903
Asai is missing?

266
00:23:21,137 --> 00:23:23,173
It hasn't been definitively
confirmed yet, but…

267
00:23:23,807 --> 00:23:26,343
Is it the same person
who got Tateiwa and Sayuri?

268
00:23:28,812 --> 00:23:30,680
We can't rule out the possibility.

269
00:23:31,381 --> 00:23:34,618
However, though I cannot share details,

270
00:23:34,684 --> 00:23:36,720
the police hold a different view.

271
00:23:39,956 --> 00:23:40,824
Mariko.

272
00:23:42,025 --> 00:23:44,294
When we went to the art museum
together recently,

273
00:23:44,861 --> 00:23:46,463
Yukimura was there too.

274
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:55,238
Is Yukimura stalking you?

275
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:58,542
Is there anything that comes to mind?

276
00:24:00,710 --> 00:24:01,845
Ah, good morning.

277
00:24:01,912 --> 00:24:04,047
Would you like
to walk to the station together?

278
00:24:05,315 --> 00:24:06,249
Mariko…

279
00:24:10,253 --> 00:24:11,421
There is, right?

280
00:24:15,959 --> 00:24:17,160
It's okay.

281
00:24:19,596 --> 00:24:21,598
I will protect you, Mariko.

282
00:25:05,375 --> 00:25:06,643
-Goodbye.
-Good day.

283
00:25:48,485 --> 00:25:51,755
I found a nice Italian place
the other day.

284
00:25:52,255 --> 00:25:54,991
-Would you like to go sometime?
-Let's see…

285
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:05,068
Thank you, everyone.

286
00:26:05,869 --> 00:26:07,237
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

287
00:26:08,104 --> 00:26:10,373
Isn't that detective
mixing business with pleasure?

288
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:12,375
He's been by Mariko's side
non-stop these past few days.

289
00:26:12,442 --> 00:26:16,212
Well, it's not a normal situation,
so I get wanting to be cautious, but…

290
00:26:39,069 --> 00:26:40,770
Thank you, everyone.

291
00:26:40,837 --> 00:26:42,439
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

292
00:26:42,505 --> 00:26:44,974
You should be the one
walking her home, Yukimura.

293
00:26:45,041 --> 00:26:46,776
What are you doing?

294
00:26:47,510 --> 00:26:49,612
Seriously, why are you just zoning out?

295
00:26:53,249 --> 00:26:55,085
No, I didn't say anything.

296
00:26:56,119 --> 00:26:58,488
It's totally obvious. Right?

297
00:26:58,555 --> 00:27:00,824
Yes. It's super easy to see.

298
00:27:01,524 --> 00:27:02,926
What's gotten into you lately?

299
00:27:04,027 --> 00:27:06,029
She hates me now…

300
00:27:06,863 --> 00:27:09,065
-That's what happened.
-What?

301
00:27:09,833 --> 00:27:11,000
Sorry.

302
00:27:27,450 --> 00:27:31,421
Lately, a lot of skincare products
for men have been coming out.

303
00:27:32,856 --> 00:27:34,390
Thanks to your influence, Mariko,

304
00:27:34,457 --> 00:27:36,760
I've started noticing those things too.

305
00:27:38,061 --> 00:27:40,230
-Back when I was young--
-Sakura.

306
00:27:41,998 --> 00:27:42,832
Yes?

307
00:27:46,169 --> 00:27:49,439
You don't need to accompany me
to work anymore.

308
00:27:54,644 --> 00:27:56,379
About what we talked about the other day…

309
00:27:57,647 --> 00:28:00,750
I agree with you that Yukimura

310
00:28:01,551 --> 00:28:05,421
has been acting a bit strangely.

311
00:28:06,756 --> 00:28:10,226
I feel a sense of discomfort,
wondering what on earth he's doing.

312
00:28:12,428 --> 00:28:13,530
But…

313
00:28:14,998 --> 00:28:18,034
he wouldn't kill anyone.

314
00:28:19,269 --> 00:28:20,470
He's not that kind of person.

315
00:28:25,241 --> 00:28:26,209
‎Is that so?

316
00:28:52,635 --> 00:28:54,137
MARIKO NOSE - DAUGHTER

317
00:28:54,204 --> 00:28:55,038
Sakura.

318
00:28:55,905 --> 00:28:58,842
Here are the tracking results
for Asai's smartphone that you asked for.

319
00:28:58,908 --> 00:28:59,809
Thank you.

320
00:29:07,650 --> 00:29:11,988
SOTA YUKIMURA

321
00:29:13,056 --> 00:29:14,891
FUNERAL OF SAYURI NOSE

322
00:29:14,958 --> 00:29:20,296
Here, O Sariputra, form is emptiness
And the very emptiness is form

323
00:29:20,363 --> 00:29:23,700
Emptiness does not differ from form
Form does not differ from emptiness

324
00:29:23,766 --> 00:29:26,236
Whatever is emptiness, that is form

325
00:29:26,302 --> 00:29:31,875
Same is true of feelings, perceptions
Impulses, and consciousness

326
00:29:31,941 --> 00:29:34,777
Here, O Sariputra
All dharmas are marked with emptiness

327
00:29:35,445 --> 00:29:37,347
They are not produced or stopped

328
00:29:37,413 --> 00:29:39,148
Not defiled or immaculate
Not deficient or complete

329
00:29:39,215 --> 00:29:41,718
Therefore, O Sariputra
In emptiness there is no form nor feeling

330
00:29:41,784 --> 00:29:44,287
Nor perception, nor impulse
Nor consciousness…

331
00:29:44,354 --> 00:29:47,023
I wonder why Yukimura didn't make it.

332
00:29:47,090 --> 00:29:48,057
RECEPTION

333
00:29:48,124 --> 00:29:50,593
Does Mariko not like him that much?

334
00:29:50,660 --> 00:29:52,095
I wonder what he did.

335
00:29:59,435 --> 00:30:01,437
-Ah…
-Ah, Izumi.

336
00:30:01,504 --> 00:30:02,572
What's up?

337
00:30:02,639 --> 00:30:05,642
Well, I figured this must be tough,
so take these if you'd like.

338
00:30:06,609 --> 00:30:07,677
Thank you.

339
00:30:11,614 --> 00:30:13,483
-Also, sorry to ask…
-Hm?

340
00:30:13,549 --> 00:30:15,251
-Could I use the toilet here?
-Yes.

341
00:30:15,985 --> 00:30:17,587
-That way, on the right.
-Thank you.

342
00:30:27,630 --> 00:30:30,266
Keito. Why don't you go
get something to eat?

343
00:30:45,548 --> 00:30:46,482
Sis…

344
00:30:47,917 --> 00:30:48,751
Hm?

345
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,789
I accidentally overheard something.

346
00:30:56,025 --> 00:30:57,493
A while before the incident,

347
00:30:58,895 --> 00:31:01,664
Mom and Dad were talking at home.

348
00:31:01,731 --> 00:31:04,200
The one who will succeed me is Mariko.

349
00:31:04,267 --> 00:31:05,969
You haven't forgotten, have you?

350
00:31:06,936 --> 00:31:10,440
That you and I share the same secret.

351
00:31:14,444 --> 00:31:15,912
The same secret?

352
00:31:17,046 --> 00:31:20,149
Were they doing something bad?

353
00:31:20,917 --> 00:31:23,319
Is that why this happened?

354
00:31:29,092 --> 00:31:35,264
FUNERAL

355
00:31:48,311 --> 00:31:49,445
Yukimura.

356
00:31:57,820 --> 00:31:58,721
Could you please

357
00:32:00,356 --> 00:32:02,759
stop approaching Mariko?

358
00:32:04,427 --> 00:32:05,762
Why is a detective saying that?

359
00:32:05,828 --> 00:32:08,865
Because I have to protect her from you.

360
00:32:10,433 --> 00:32:12,869
I could arrest you.

361
00:32:14,437 --> 00:32:18,641
What you are doing is stalking.

362
00:32:21,044 --> 00:32:22,078
Normally, it requires that

363
00:32:22,678 --> 00:32:26,416
the other party be aware
they are being followed,

364
00:32:26,482 --> 00:32:30,653
but if the conduct is judged objectively
to cause anxiety,

365
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:32,722
it can fall under "stalking",

366
00:32:34,323 --> 00:32:36,392
even if the other party is unaware.

367
00:32:38,027 --> 00:32:39,028
In other words,

368
00:32:40,363 --> 00:32:42,832
regardless of what Mariko thinks,

369
00:32:44,500 --> 00:32:45,868
you can be punished.

370
00:32:49,439 --> 00:32:51,140
Since what age?

371
00:32:52,308 --> 00:32:57,880
You have been continually committing
criminal acts all this time.

372
00:33:00,349 --> 00:33:01,184
Am I wrong?

373
00:33:07,757 --> 00:33:08,891
-I…
-Hm?

374
00:33:11,461 --> 00:33:13,262
You didn't intend to?

375
00:33:15,465 --> 00:33:20,403
Most people who commit crimes
probably didn't intend to,

376
00:33:21,571 --> 00:33:22,972
either.

377
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:30,246
A life ruined by a brief impulse.

378
00:33:31,581 --> 00:33:34,383
Other than that,
it was a completely stainless life.

379
00:33:39,255 --> 00:33:40,990
If only you hadn't loved her…

380
00:33:43,226 --> 00:33:45,628
you wouldn't have ended up a criminal.

381
00:33:57,974 --> 00:34:00,776
What's with that detective?
Calling you a stalker.

382
00:34:01,377 --> 00:34:04,881
It's not like
you forced yourself on Mariko.

383
00:34:05,681 --> 00:34:07,750
But it was something
I shouldn't have done.

384
00:34:11,287 --> 00:34:14,056
Besides, you've been protecting
Mariko all this time, right?

385
00:34:14,957 --> 00:34:16,859
Which is why you ended up a suspect.

386
00:34:16,926 --> 00:34:17,760
It's fine.

387
00:34:18,928 --> 00:34:21,164
It's what I chose to do.

388
00:34:23,633 --> 00:34:26,168
Besides, from Mariko's perspective,
I really am creepy.

389
00:34:28,337 --> 00:34:30,339
So this situation
is just an effect of that.

390
00:34:32,141 --> 00:34:33,476
-But still…
-It's fine.

391
00:34:40,149 --> 00:34:41,417
Yes, you're okay.

392
00:34:42,451 --> 00:34:44,153
Don't fall asleep! Take off your shoes.

393
00:34:45,154 --> 00:34:47,657
-Take them off.
-Do it yourself.

394
00:34:47,723 --> 00:34:49,892
-You're fine like that?
-Yes, cover me, please.

395
00:34:49,959 --> 00:34:50,893
-Okay.
-Thanks.

396
00:34:55,298 --> 00:34:57,533
You know you can't hold your liquor…

397
00:35:37,940 --> 00:35:39,275
PICTURE DIARY

398
00:35:56,025 --> 00:35:59,829
The President has decided
to delay the launch event.

399
00:36:00,696 --> 00:36:04,767
Then it won't
make it in time for the release.

400
00:36:04,834 --> 00:36:06,636
I won't let everyone's
hard work go to waste.

401
00:36:07,403 --> 00:36:08,804
I will protect it.

402
00:36:09,739 --> 00:36:11,374
All right, let's do it!

403
00:36:12,875 --> 00:36:14,610
-Let's do it, shall we?
-Yes.

404
00:36:14,677 --> 00:36:15,511
Thank you.

405
00:36:19,682 --> 00:36:21,083
Hello.

406
00:36:25,454 --> 00:36:29,625
I told them that, but will
we really be able to release it?

407
00:36:30,393 --> 00:36:32,361
What if we can't…

408
00:36:34,463 --> 00:36:35,965
It's rare for you to be like this.

409
00:36:39,268 --> 00:36:45,241
I thought I had a pretty lucky life.

410
00:36:48,944 --> 00:36:50,746
But maybe I was wrong?

411
00:36:58,921 --> 00:36:59,922
2 MARIKO NOSE

412
00:36:59,989 --> 00:37:01,657
No way, I beat Nose!

413
00:37:01,724 --> 00:37:03,526
-Yay!
-Yay!

414
00:37:03,592 --> 00:37:05,728
Look, look. I got 873.

415
00:37:05,795 --> 00:37:07,096
Amazing.

416
00:37:07,163 --> 00:37:08,397
-That's nuts.
-You worked hard.

417
00:37:48,904 --> 00:37:51,440
It's a good product, so if we
launch it, customers will follow.

418
00:37:51,507 --> 00:37:52,375
Yukimura.

419
00:37:53,109 --> 00:37:55,945
It's got to be now, for the sake
of the company's turnaround.

420
00:37:56,011 --> 00:37:57,980
-You're causing trouble…
-I understand how you feel,

421
00:37:58,481 --> 00:37:59,749
but now is not the time.

422
00:38:01,917 --> 00:38:03,419
There's meaning in us
pioneering and deploying this

423
00:38:03,486 --> 00:38:05,988
before other companies
release similar products.

424
00:38:06,055 --> 00:38:07,223
Please.

425
00:38:10,726 --> 00:38:11,694
‎Hey.

426
00:38:12,928 --> 00:38:14,163
-What are you doing?
-Manager…

427
00:38:15,398 --> 00:38:16,332
Come here.

428
00:38:22,972 --> 00:38:23,939
Uh, Mariko…

429
00:38:29,578 --> 00:38:30,813
What are you doing?

430
00:38:32,248 --> 00:38:33,082
Seriously,

431
00:38:34,250 --> 00:38:35,985
what is going on? What is your intention?

432
00:38:37,119 --> 00:38:37,953
I'm sorry.

433
00:38:41,524 --> 00:38:44,794
Have you always been sneaking around
doing things behind my back like this?

434
00:38:46,729 --> 00:38:48,164
Doing things on your own

435
00:38:48,230 --> 00:38:50,966
without my knowledge,
claiming it was for me?

436
00:38:58,073 --> 00:38:59,775
I always thought it was strange.

437
00:39:04,580 --> 00:39:07,116
The four-leaf clover left for me…

438
00:39:09,852 --> 00:39:13,522
The adhesive bandage
during the summer festival.

439
00:39:19,795 --> 00:39:20,696
Was that what it was?

440
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:27,002
Whenever things weren't going well for me,

441
00:39:27,870 --> 00:39:29,205
or when bad things happened,

442
00:39:30,206 --> 00:39:33,175
assuming I might be feeling down
and acting ahead of time…

443
00:39:33,242 --> 00:39:35,578
-Was that what you were doing?
-No…

444
00:39:36,512 --> 00:39:38,547
That's just creepy!

445
00:39:38,614 --> 00:39:40,082
All of it is creepy!

446
00:39:41,550 --> 00:39:43,953
Your excessive kindness,

447
00:39:44,653 --> 00:39:47,423
your consideration,
all of it is out of line!

448
00:39:52,928 --> 00:39:56,699
When did I ever ask you to protect me?

449
00:40:04,139 --> 00:40:05,274
Don't you decide

450
00:40:06,709 --> 00:40:10,045
what's for my sake
or what my happiness is!

451
00:40:13,616 --> 00:40:14,450
I'm sorry.

452
00:40:17,987 --> 00:40:18,854
I won't forgive you.

453
00:40:22,224 --> 00:40:24,593
If you leave my side,
I will never forgive you!

454
00:40:28,397 --> 00:40:29,331
I will never…

455
00:40:32,067 --> 00:40:33,068
forgive you.

456
00:40:57,026 --> 00:40:59,261
From Mariko's perspective,
I really am creepy.

457
00:41:00,663 --> 00:41:02,598
So this situation
is just an effect of that.

458
00:41:03,566 --> 00:41:04,767
-But still…
-It's fine.

459
00:41:07,503 --> 00:41:11,907
I just want Mariko to smile and be happy.

460
00:41:17,112 --> 00:41:19,515
I kept thinking about
what I could do for her…

461
00:41:22,351 --> 00:41:24,787
but me disappearing
is what's best for Mariko.

462
00:41:32,394 --> 00:41:35,130
That's how I can protect
Mariko's happiness.

463
00:42:21,143 --> 00:42:22,077
Here you go.

464
00:42:24,113 --> 00:42:25,014
Thank you!

465
00:42:29,018 --> 00:42:29,952
Mom!

466
00:42:32,087 --> 00:42:34,256
Oh, Mariko, welcome back!

467
00:42:41,063 --> 00:42:41,897
Here.

468
00:42:44,033 --> 00:42:46,001
Thank you!

469
00:42:47,036 --> 00:42:48,871
-You got these for me?
-Yes!

470
00:42:50,272 --> 00:42:51,407
So pretty.

471
00:42:52,675 --> 00:42:53,575
Wanna go home?

472
00:42:55,511 --> 00:42:57,046
Did you walk here alone?

473
00:42:57,112 --> 00:43:00,182
-Yes, that's right.
-Wow, that's amazing.

474
00:43:52,434 --> 00:43:53,902
You bastard.

475
00:43:53,969 --> 00:43:59,374
You take advantage
when people try to be nice to you!

476
00:44:12,755 --> 00:44:14,957
If you don't know anything,

477
00:44:15,023 --> 00:44:17,259
there's no point in keeping you alive.

478
00:44:20,295 --> 00:44:21,697
Yukimura!

479
00:44:23,198 --> 00:44:24,433
Sota Yukimura.

480
00:44:25,467 --> 00:44:28,971
-Huh?
-The boy you're looking for…

481
00:44:30,005 --> 00:44:31,173
is at our company.

482
00:44:32,341 --> 00:44:33,609
His name is Sota Yukimura.

483
00:44:59,268 --> 00:45:01,436
Yukimura, why?

484
00:45:01,503 --> 00:45:03,505
‎NEXT TIME…

485
00:45:08,076 --> 00:45:09,011
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

